cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "MacroShock: a reproducible multi-asset stress-testing and factor-attribution engine"
abstract: >-
  MacroShock is an open-source computational platform for multi-asset portfolio stress testing.
  It decomposes portfolio losses by risk factor and holding under regime-conditional covariance,
  quantifies tail risk with fat-tailed estimators, measures benchmark-relative active risk, and
  solves for the most plausible joint factor shock producing a target loss. Analyses are expressed
  as declarative YAML workflows and run identically on a laptop, in a container, or on a
  Kubernetes/REANA cluster, making results reproducible from a pinned data snapshot.
type: software
